codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s lazy global-domination relation. The paper defines the relation and its polynomial scan in Section 2, while Section 3.2 warns that random \(G(n,p)^k\) instances often become easy—so the prior planted-clique hypothesis was discarded. [Full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1408.6485v1).

Key results:

- All local gates pass.
- Planted witnesses: 12/12 verified.
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Six adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, averaging 3,231,947 operations and 0.412 seconds.
- Compact symmetry route: at most 79 operations.
- Answer size: seven integers, 61 characters.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/gen_1408_6485.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/README.md)
- [Blocked status](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/BLOCKED.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1408.6485/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only blocker is external: both hardening attempts and both G9 arms received OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Those errors are preserved and correctly do not count as model failures. A funded OpenRouter key is required to obtain the final four-vendor hardness verdict.
